  "question": {
    "text": "The line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is a tangent to the circle at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and the centre of the circle lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then, the radius of the circle is:"
